  "worked_solution": "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x-3<0\n$$\n\n \n\nis a \"*less than*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-2x-3\n$$\n\nis *below *the $x$-axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13972108/assets/aa7d7e5bf2e6572b08161b824bc1e27d5ebec518ccd00734cc78a7dcf320505b.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $-3<x<2.$",
